# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AISHA4SENATE — Environment Variables
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# HOW TO USE:
# 1. Copy this file and rename it  .env.local  for local development
# 2. In Vercel dashboard → your project → Settings → Environment Variables
#    Add each variable below with its real value
# 3. NEVER commit .env.local to GitHub — it's already in .gitignore
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# AIRTABLE
# ─────────
# Your Personal Access Token (PAT)
# Get it at: airtable.com → Account → Developer Hub → Personal Access Tokens
# Required scopes: data.records:write  and  schema.bases:read
AIRTABLE_PAT=your_airtable_personal_access_token_here

# Your Base ID
# Find it: open your base → Help → API Documentation → top of page shows "The ID of this base is appXXXXXXXX"
AIRTABLE_BASE_ID=appXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TABLE NAMES (must match EXACTLY what you named them in Airtable)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   Table 1:  Volunteers
#   Table 2:  Town Hall Requests
#   Table 3:  Newsletter Subscribers
#
# These are already hardcoded in the api/ functions above.
# If you name your tables differently, update the table names
# inside api/volunteer.js, api/townhall.js, api/newsletter.js
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL: Add more secrets here as the campaign grows
# e.g. email service API key, analytics, payment gateway, etc.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
